// Temporaless v1 read-only inspection contract.
//
// `RunInspectionService` answers the questions an operator console asks of a
// record store without writing, repairing, claiming, or deleting anything.
// Every method is implementable directly over a bucket store with bounded
// listings and point reads; none needs a cross-run index.
//
// Temporaless keeps point records, not an event journal. The history and
// pending state in `DescribeRunResponse` are derived at read time from record
// timestamps and statuses. They are evidence, not a replayable log:
// overwritten intermediate states and released claims are not visible, and a
// status the records cannot evidence (cancel, terminate, timeout) never
